knext bundled fix for vinext 1.0.1 (dist output)
Upstream: https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/pull/3771 (issue https://github.com/cloudflare/vinext/issues/3428)
What it fixes: in an app with both app/ and pages/, a Pages route that resolves to `notFound`
(getStaticProps/getServerSideProps `notFound`, or a `fallback: false` miss) rendered pages/404,
or the Pages error page when there is none. Next.js renders the App Router not-found in that case:
with the app directory enabled it looks up /_not-found before /404 (Next.js deploy tests
not-found-with-pages-i18n and pages-router-app-not-found).
The hybrid bridge now asks the Pages renderer to mark a document 404 that came from a notFound
result (`x-vinext-pages-not-found`; middleware cannot set it). The App request handler consumes
the marker and renders its not-found in place, keeping the source route's Cache-Control as
Next.js does. Data requests, pages that render themselves with a 404 status, and apps without
an app/ directory are unchanged. Dev is unchanged (it renders hybrid Pages separately).
Port difference: upstream exports the header name from server/headers.js and moves the
unmatched-route not-found render into a shared helper. Here each file declares the header name
locally and the unmatched-route branch is left as it is (vinext-3682 edits it); a copy of the
not-found render sits beside renderPagesForMatchKind. Same behaviour.
Retire: delete this file (and its manifest entry) when the pinned vinext is >= the first
release that includes cloudflare/vinext#3771.
Applied by `knext vinext-patches` (runs from the app's postinstall and before `knext build`).

